window.products.push({"id":241106,"name":"(Pack of 20)-Yerbero - Premium 4 Inches Long California Blue Prairie Sage | 20 Hand Tied Bundles Smudging Kit for Home Cleansing, Meditation. Purifyin","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":29.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/711ULW4kE1L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"HOW TO PURIFY THE HOUSE WITH SAGE. Sage is highly valued in herbal medicine to care for the mouth, throat and hormonal health. But we can also burn it or use the essential oil to purify the air in the home. 4 STEPS TO PURIFY THE HOUSE WITH SALVIA The ritual of purifying a space with the smoke of a sacred plant is a universal practice. Salvia officinalis is one of the most used plants for this purpose, usually for energy purposes, but its properties justify it: its essential oils have proven their ability to enhance intellectual abilities. Smelling a space with sage favors mental clarity, joy and calm. To burn the sage and purify the house, follow these steps: Preparation: You need a bunch of dried sage tied with cotton, a bowl to catch the ash, and a feather or fan. In some places you will find a bundle of sage already prepared, which you can burn like an incense stick. Lighting: Light the sage inside the bowl, blow on the fire and let it go out. Watch out for sparks! Smudge: you can bring the smoke closer to the people who participate in the ritual. Direct it to the head, arms, legs, back... Cleansing: Slowly walk the space with the bowl, dispersing the smoke with the feather. Make it go where your intuition guides you. Blue sage is a relative of the well-known white sage. With a thin leaf, it owes its name to its indigo flowers. It can be used to accompany meditation or simply to enjoy its fragrance and relax. It is also burned during purification and protection rituals. It is said that it helps connect with abundance and prosperity and that it favors spiritual development and inner strength. Celtic druids used it to increase their wisdom and during their healing and protection rituals. Many Native American cultures smoked with sage to purify body and spirit.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/711ULW4kE1L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"YERBERO","source_asin":"B0BQ93XCZK","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-241106","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BQ93XCZK","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B0BQ93XCZK","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
